Shape of the parity unit (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:telemetry/SignalsWorkspace)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
requiredCount=58 = 11 panels + 4 data-states + 43 strings. 0 charts, 0 maps. Data sources (4):
usePinned (GET /pinned), useSignalDiffServer (GET /signals/{id}/diff), useSignals (GET
/signals/{id}/available), useTogglePin (POST /pinned + DELETE /pinned/{id}). The web page is a thin
orchestrator composing seven shared telemetry components inside a PageContainer; the native port
reproduces the whole tree and composes the already-ported shared surfaces (SignalSelector,
SignalCompareControls, SignalStatsPanel, SignalChartPanel) rather than re-implementing them.

Native realisation (Fluent / WinUI 3, ADR-002/004/005/006/011/013/014/015)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
- SignalsWorkspacePage : UserControl — mounts the shared PageContainer (CopyLink="Share", the live
  connection TsBadge in the header Actions) whose PageContent is the full workspace tree: the load-failed
  TsAlertBanner, the no-vehicle TsEmptyState, the four headline TsStatCards, the "Add signals" TsAccordion
  hosting the shared SignalSelector catalog, the workspace toolbar TsGlassPanel (Time Range / Per Page /
  Run / Live / Compare + the live/compare TsHelpTooltip), the Compare section (SignalCompareControls, the
  four diff TsStatCards, the bulk-actions toolbar, and the diff TsGlassPanel with its loading-skeleton /
  no-changes / error / rows + pinned-chips branches), the Live/Historical section (SignalStatsPanel, the
  chart-layout tabs, SignalChartPanel, and the "pick signals and run a query" empty TsGlassPanel) and the
  catalog-refresh footer. Thin renderer: every label/value/visibility flows from SignalsWorkspaceDisplay;
  PropertyChanged is marshalled onto the UI thread; Group automation peer; tokens only (no literal colours).
- SignalsWorkspacePageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged — UI-thread-free state holder. Reads the catalog
  (useSignals) + pins (usePinned) through ISignalsWorkspaceFeed, fetches the diff on Compare mode
  (useSignalDiffServer), owns the pin/unpin flow (useTogglePin) and the mutually-exclusive Live/Compare
  toggles, exposes UpdateLiveState (the P1/S4 SSE seam feeding the live-rate card + connection badge), and
  projects SignalsWorkspaceDisplay. LoadAsync/RefreshAsync/LoadDiffAsync + superseding CTS; no I/O in the view.
- SignalsWorkspaceProjection / SignalsWorkspaceModel / SignalsWorkspaceDisplay — pure projection (no WinUI
  types) resolving all 43 i18n keys on every call (the conditionally-rendered keys are pre-resolved so a
  single projection requests the whole manifest set), the eight stat-card values (fmtInt port), the
  window-span cell, the pinned-first diff rows (reusing the shared SignalDiffProjection), and the
  catalog/diff data-state flags. SignalsWorkspaceRegistration — RouteName="SignalsWorkspace" (matches
  RouteTable.cs Page("SignalsWorkspace","signals",TelemetrySignals)), Slug, the five generated operation
  ids and the per-vehicle pin context. PII-safe SignalsWorkspaceDiagnostics (view.opened only).
- ISignalsWorkspaceFeed / EmptySignalsWorkspaceFeed (no-backend default the shell-registered page mounts
  against) / SignalsWorkspaceClientFeed (the generated-OpenAPI-client adapter, ADR-004). Like the sibling
  SignalDiffTableSource, the diff + pinned reads omit the web query parameters because the generated
  /pinned and /signals/{id}/diff descriptors declare none (the contract client rejects undeclared ones) —
  the diff relies on the backend default trailing-hour window and the pinned list is filtered to signal
  rows client-side; each pin write still carries the per-vehicle diff context.
- Shell registration: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers
  PageFactory.Register("SignalsWorkspace", () => new FeatureViews.Telemetry.SignalsWorkspacePage()).

i18n note (R3/ADR-014)
----------------------
The 43 manifest keys are resolved through keyed ILocalizer.GetString(key, <web default>) flowing through
ShellLocalizer -> shell Localization (resw lookup -> English fallback), exactly as the web resolves the
inline t(key, default) fallbacks. Zero hardcoded literals; the auto-generated resw is left untouched.

